  "behavior": [
    "Issued cleanup revokes only the exact owned credential and requires fresh REVOKED inventory plus exact application identity/readback; applicationWithdrawn remains false and applicationHistoryPreserved is explicit.",
    "Unused offer cleanup requires exact revoked authenticated detail, no issued_at and no issued credential; approved/unknown/inflight or failed/expired-but-unrevoked outcomes remain incomplete.",
    "D01 and D04 readiness require credentialRevoked, applicationHistoryPreserved and complete cleanup.",
    "D05 recovery preserves the captured application and run marker, reuses canonical operator /issue, tracks exact retired transaction tuples, and requires a new pending transaction and fresh offer contents/code.",
    "Every historical exclusion is freshly proved from scoped transaction detail plus credential inventory; the original strict selectors and first-run duplicate protection are unchanged.",
    "Foreign, active, issued, unknown extra, ambiguous, hidden/withdrawn application and uncertain mutation states cannot authorize completion; a lost response resolves only through strict public readback."
  ],
  "boundaries": [
    "These are isolated source regressions and local configuration checks, not Canvas/beta/signing/wallet/live runtime qualification.",
    "Same-application reissue is sequential and is not claimed to be a globally atomic cancel/reissue transaction.",
    "The retained history path supports unused canceled offers only; issued credential history is not silently excluded.",
    "No application sweep, same-template mutation, release-manifest qualification change, deployment change, runtime receipt, or successful capture is introduced."
  ],
